          "jcr:created": "Tue Sep 16 2025 20:35:54 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<h3>Speakers:</h3>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Chris Kroboth</b>, MS, FP-C</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Jeffrey Goodloe</b>, MD, FACEP</span><br>\n&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Sep 16 2025 20:37:19 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_908007915_copy_": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "text": "<h1><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Webinar: With or without capnography? How your assessment tools could change everything</span></span></span></h1>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Capnography is often treated as a tool reserved for respiratory-specific cases, while pulse oximetry and non-invasive blood pressure take the lead during initial assessments. But what if that order is steering you in the wrong direction?</span></p>\n<div><p><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">This interactive, case-based webinar will challenge traditional approaches by presenting real-world medical and trauma scenarios—first without capnography, and then with it. You’ll see how access to EtCO₂ data can shift your clinical impression, change your treatment decisions, and ultimately lead to better patient outcomes. This free on-demand webinar was presented by EMS1.com, Medtronic and Stryker.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>You will learn:</b></span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Why starting with capnography—not saving it for later—can uncover critical patient changes earlier.</span></span></span></li>\n<li><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">How EtCO₂ trends can reveal what other vitals might miss during both trauma and medical calls.</span></span></span></li>\n<li><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span data-rte-class=\"rte-temp\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Practical ways to integrate capnography into your default assessment workflow for all patient types.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Sep 18 2025 20:54:03 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
